steps.message:
The fix is complete and verified. Summary of changes:

**`src/offering/entities/offeringPackage.entity.ts`**
1. Added `Offering.billableQuantity()` — turns a dimension's aggregated usage into the quantity the customer actually owes for:
   - no allowance → all usage is chargeable;
   - `inf` allowance → nothing (can never be exhausted);
   - allowance not used up in full (usage ≤ allowance) → nothing;
   - plan forbids overage (`overageAllowed` not `true`, including absent) → nothing;
   - otherwise only the usage past the finite, exhausted allowance.
2. Added `Offering.shouldAddUsageLineItem()` — a dimension gets a line when the customer owes something on it; a dimension priced at zero also gets a line unless the business' invoice settings (`freeDimensionOnInvoice: hide`) hide free dimensions.
3. The non-tiered dimension path in `getLineItemsForUsage` now stores the owed quantity (allowance applied) in `dimensionTotals`, so a line reports the quantity owed for even where the price is zero, treats a dimension with an allowance but no price as free (was producing `NaN` unit costs), and skips lines the rules above exclude.

**`src/offering/entities/offeringAllowance.entity.spec.ts`** (new) — 12 unit tests covering all allowance/overage combinations, both invoice settings, and quantity reporting.

